    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;lie on the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, for some&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>.&nbsp;The shortest distance of&nbsp;&nbsp;the plane from the origin is:",
